Notes from audit/ files: openOODA/audit/wasm_sk1.oot, wasm_sk2.oot, wasm_pipe.oot, wasm_arch.oot, wasm_qa.oot are the loop-6 phalanx audit rollup. The five wasm_emit_* files above are the loop-6 detectors named in wasm_sk2.oot section 1. x86_emit_harv.oo follows in glob order; x86 is the next emit lane after WASM. llvm_emit_*.oo and aarch64_emit_*.oo follow. SHIPPED.oot line 35 names aarch64 as side-ELF only, not a current cycle task.

Status: ACTIVE. The compiler owner is on the WASM emit loop-6 phalanx. X86 is mid-cycle (Cycle B harvest per x86_phalanx.oot section 0). LLVM is also active. The owner statement "agents working on the compilers" matches disk: WASM, x86, and LLVM emits are all in flight. AArch64 is residual. No Windows emit file exists yet. The plan name `emit_windows.oo` from win_compiler_plan.oot section 1 has no analog on disk.

Conflict with Windows lane: low. The compiler owner has not started Windows emit. SHIPPED.oot line 34 keeps the emit-x86 overlay pin, so the compiler tree is sensitive to a parallel Windows edit. Phase 1 should wait for the WASM loop-6 phalanx to close before adding emit_windows.oo.

## 2. Runtime lane

