Notes: chs_rt_wasm_print.c and chs_rt_wasm.c are the WASM runtime files. The header in chs_rt_wasm_print.c line 2 says it is the WASI fd_write body. chs_rt_fs.c and chs_rt_sys.c are general fs and sys support. chs_rt_landlock.c, chs_rt_rlimit.c, chs_rt_caps.c are the capability surface named in SHIPPED.oot section 2.

Status: ACTIVE. The runtime owner is on WASM runtime in lockstep with the compiler WASM emit. The audit openOODA/audit/plan_llvm_rt.oot (line 5: "Did not edit c_emit. No runtime C edit.") is older; the current phalanx is WASM-side, not LLVM. Landlock and rlimit shims are named as the two POSIX-isms that need a Windows port (win_chs_rt_posix_audit.oot). Landlock is also being worked on the std side; see sec/sys/landlock_engine.oo in section 3.

Conflict with Windows lane: medium. The runtime owner is the blocker for Phase 2 (chs_rt Windows port). Per the plan, the owner must produce chs_rt_win32_*.c shims. The owner is busy with WASM today. Phase 2 cannot start until the WASM runtime loop closes, or until the owner names a Windows sub-lane.

