Status: ACTIVE. The std owner is on a security/sandbox refactor (M172 split). Landlock work in std ties to the runtime Landlock file (section 2). ROADMAP.oot line 72 says residual must not be sold as product; std hits that line through audit_engine and landlock_engine. The std tree is shared with Windows per ROADMAP.oot line 83: "Not a second std". So the std lane is in scope for the Windows work, but it is not a Windows-only refactor.

Conflict with Windows lane: low. The M172 split is sandbox plumbing, not Windows-bound. The owner has not started a Windows-only std file. The std tree is the lane Windows shares, not the lane Windows replaces.

